# SIS Core Conventions

Read `.cursor/brain/PROJECT.md` for full context.

## Stack
Laravel 13 + Inertia/React + PostgreSQL + Redis. Reference architecture in `.cursor/architecture/`.

## Non-Negotiable Rules
1. Every academic operation scoped to `academic_year_id`
2. Never hard-delete official academic records — use status + effective_to
3. Heavy ops (bulk import, certificates, reports) via Laravel Queue — never in HTTP request
4. PostgreSQL = source of truth; Redis = cache only
5. No manual DB changes — always versioned migrations
6. No `SELECT *` in production API queries
7. No N+1 queries — eager load relationships
8. Idempotency keys for payments, imports, certificates, notifications
9. Correlation ID on every request for audit tracing
10. Measure slow queries with EXPLAIN ANALYZE before adding indexes
11. DO NOT OPTIMIZE FOR A NUMBER — optimize for measured workload (DATABASE-ADAPTIVE-GOVERNANCE.md)
12. Every optimization requires before/after evidence (PERFORMANCE-BUDGET.md)
13. PostgreSQL = source of truth — intelligence layer recommends only, never auto-modifies schema (DATABASE-INTELLIGENCE-LAYER.md)
14. Self-Healing: Tier 1 safe ops only — pool resize, replica routing (SELF-HEALING-RUNBOOK.md)

## Data Types (PostgreSQL)
- PKs: `BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY`
- Status: `SMALLINT` (not TINYINT)
- Money: `NUMERIC(12,2)`
- Timestamps: `TIMESTAMPTZ`

## Module Implementation Order
organization → academic → security → students → enrollment → curriculum → teachers → attendance → exams → lifecycle modules

## 45K Baseline (20 schools, 10 years)
- 45,000 active students = **baseline**, not architectural ceiling
- Partition attendance.records from year 1 at baseline (P0) — re-evaluate if volume drops
- daily_section_summary required for dashboards (P0)
- Batch writes for attendance — never row-by-row (batch-write-patterns.md)
- Phase 2 infra from launch: PgBouncer + Read Replica
- Capacity: `.cursor/architecture/capacity-planning.md` (dynamic model)
- Adaptive rules: `.cursor/architecture/DATABASE-ADAPTIVE-GOVERNANCE.md`
- Implementation: `.cursor/architecture/WORK-PLAN.md`

## Database Changes — MANDATORY
Any DB change MUST follow: database-change/SKILL.md → schema-change-impact.md → DATABASE-CHANGE-CHECKLIST.md → update database-blueprint.md

